1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Last time on Zombieland Saga, we found out we're doing a show for 500 people!

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
And once I realized it might bring back some memories of my past, I got super hyped about it!

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
But then Kotaro decided to have us train in the mountains for some reason,

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
and I may have gotten a little upset that everyone was focusing on survival instead of rehearsal.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
But then I learned a valuable lesson when I realized that working together like that made them way more in sync as performers!

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Turns out I was the one who lost my head, literally!

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
And just when I decided it was better to put that energy into being a good friend and working toward the future,

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
a truck flew by out of nowhere and knocked the hype right out of me!

9
00:02:07,002 --> 00:02:21,122
What was I doing?

10
00:02:29,122 --> 00:02:31,482
What is this place?

11
00:02:37,002 --> 00:02:46,102
Oh, oh, oh, oh?

12
00:02:46,102 --> 00:02:47,722
Ah, oh, oh, oh, oh.

13
00:02:47,722 --> 00:02:52,982
Ah, oh, ah, oh.

14
00:02:57,942 --> 00:03:02,982
The Spidey Elliott Laughíamosfire.

15
00:03:02,982 --> 00:03:08,102
I'm so sorry.

16
00:03:08,822 --> 00:03:10,262
What in the hell?

17
00:03:18,662 --> 00:03:19,382
Sakura?

18
00:03:20,022 --> 00:03:22,162
It looks like you finally woke up.

19
00:03:22,202 --> 00:03:22,782
That's good.

20
00:03:25,982 --> 00:03:26,782
Easy.

21
00:03:27,382 --> 00:03:29,702
Hey, what's wrong?

22
00:03:32,982 --> 00:03:44,862
You okay?

23
00:03:45,222 --> 00:03:45,602
Uh-oh.

24
00:03:45,902 --> 00:03:47,382
I think she lost her mind.

25
00:03:54,382 --> 00:03:56,982
I can't...

26
00:03:56,982 --> 00:03:58,482
Sakura!

27
00:03:58,482 --> 00:04:01,502
It doesn't matter what I do.

28
00:04:01,562 --> 00:04:02,362
It won't work.

29
00:04:02,982 --> 00:04:04,682
There's no point in trying.

30
00:04:06,102 --> 00:04:07,782
I'm all out of guesses here.

31
00:04:08,302 --> 00:04:10,342
I think she's afraid of us or something.

32
00:04:10,782 --> 00:04:12,702
Perhaps a slap to the face will help.

33
00:04:12,822 --> 00:04:13,342
Hang on.

34
00:04:13,582 --> 00:04:14,342
I might know.

35
00:04:16,862 --> 00:04:26,942
You see?

36
00:04:26,942 --> 00:04:27,942
Stop!

37
00:04:27,942 --> 00:04:31,302
I'm not capable of anything.

38
00:04:35,302 --> 00:04:36,422
What just happened?

39
00:04:36,422 --> 00:04:37,662
Oh, God!

40
00:04:37,662 --> 00:04:38,302
You're up.

41
00:04:38,302 --> 00:04:40,302
I'm Mizuno?

42
00:04:40,302 --> 00:04:41,502
In the flesh?

43
00:04:41,502 --> 00:04:44,482
Wait, what are you doing here?

44
00:04:45,982 --> 00:04:47,962
Look, do you remember what your name is?

45
00:04:48,082 --> 00:04:49,662
Uh, my name?

46
00:04:49,822 --> 00:04:50,382
It's Sakura.

47
00:04:50,662 --> 00:04:53,122
Your address, your phone number, and your family?

48
00:04:53,342 --> 00:04:53,802
All that?

49
00:04:55,102 --> 00:04:56,902
Well, yeah, of course.

50
00:04:57,302 --> 00:04:57,842
I see.

51
00:04:59,562 --> 00:05:02,202
Hey, you're I from Iron Frill, aren't you?

52
00:05:02,642 --> 00:05:03,422
Big fan.

53
00:05:03,962 --> 00:05:04,342
Sakura.

54
00:05:04,582 --> 00:05:04,942
Yes?

55
00:05:04,942 --> 00:05:10,762
I can explain everything that happened to you, but you're probably not gonna like what you hear.

56
00:05:11,522 --> 00:05:13,042
So please stay calm.

57
00:05:14,002 --> 00:05:17,182
See, you're kind of a zombie.

58
00:05:19,902 --> 00:05:20,542
What?

59
00:05:21,322 --> 00:05:22,942
Come on, that's not...

60
00:05:22,942 --> 00:05:27,422
Ten years back, you died. Not sure how.

61
00:05:28,582 --> 00:05:29,762
No way.

62
00:05:49,522 --> 00:05:51,522
What's gonna happen to her now?

63
00:05:51,522 --> 00:05:54,722
I'm certain Lady Ai's doing everything she can.

64
00:05:56,262 --> 00:05:56,742
Damn.

65
00:05:57,302 --> 00:05:59,582
Where the hell is Shades at a time like this?

66
00:05:59,702 --> 00:06:00,342
He's out.

67
00:06:00,682 --> 00:06:03,762
He left this morning saying there was a business errand he needed to run.

68
00:06:04,722 --> 00:06:05,042
Huh?

69
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:06,762
Well?

70
00:06:07,022 --> 00:06:07,662
What's up?

71
00:06:07,962 --> 00:06:08,882
Is Sakura okay?

72
00:06:09,262 --> 00:06:09,662
Yeah.

73
00:06:10,882 --> 00:06:11,802
Here's the thing.

74
00:06:12,762 --> 00:06:16,502
Getting hit by that truck yesterday made all her real-life memories come back.

75
00:06:16,602 --> 00:06:17,102
Say what?

76
00:06:17,262 --> 00:06:18,322
But that's not all.

77
00:06:18,322 --> 00:06:22,402
Now she doesn't remember anything that happened after she became a zombie.

78
00:06:23,122 --> 00:06:23,922
Not good.

79
00:06:24,282 --> 00:06:24,762
I know.

80
00:06:25,022 --> 00:06:26,742
I've tried to explain some things.

81
00:06:27,242 --> 00:06:29,322
I told her about us being the undead.

82
00:06:29,802 --> 00:06:31,282
And about Franshushu.

83
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:35,922
Hey, these are the other girls I was telling you about before.

84
00:06:35,922 --> 00:06:44,982
You mean you really don't remember our group, Sakura?

85
00:06:45,242 --> 00:06:46,922
Uh, I don't...

86
00:06:47,602 --> 00:06:48,422
Wait a sec.

87
00:06:48,742 --> 00:06:50,582
Does this mean she can't be in the show?

88
00:06:51,502 --> 00:06:52,122
The show?

89
00:06:53,122 --> 00:06:53,522
Um...

90
00:06:53,522 --> 00:06:56,542
It's their first solo concert for 500 people.

91
00:06:56,702 --> 00:06:57,002
Huh?

92
00:06:57,322 --> 00:07:00,062
It's in just a few days at a place called Arapino.

93
00:07:02,182 --> 00:07:02,742
Arapino?

94
00:07:03,282 --> 00:07:04,522
Yeah, it's a big deal.

95
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:06,562
A total turning point for our group.

96
00:07:08,462 --> 00:07:09,522
I think I...

97
00:07:09,522 --> 00:07:17,722
So you see, all of us have practiced really hard.

98
00:07:18,342 --> 00:07:19,042
And you too.

99
00:07:19,702 --> 00:07:21,942
I'm sure you're really confused right now.

100
00:07:22,622 --> 00:07:24,762
But when the time comes, I know you'll be ready.

101
00:07:26,682 --> 00:07:27,162
Wow.

102
00:07:27,162 --> 00:07:29,602
Oh, I really did become an idol.

103
00:07:37,502 --> 00:07:37,982
No.

104
00:07:38,562 --> 00:07:40,222
You guys can do it without me.

105
00:07:40,622 --> 00:07:41,982
Come on, you'll be fine.

106
00:07:42,202 --> 00:07:44,222
If you practice, I bet it'll come right back.

107
00:07:44,382 --> 00:07:44,642
Cool.

108
00:07:44,782 --> 00:07:46,662
I'm telling you, I can't do it.

109
00:07:46,842 --> 00:07:48,522
You don't know until you try.

110
00:07:48,562 --> 00:07:49,542
I don't want to.

111
00:07:50,962 --> 00:07:54,602
Because working for something and succeeding...

112
00:07:54,602 --> 00:07:57,762
Well, I just don't have what it takes.

113
00:07:58,362 --> 00:07:59,462
Have what it takes?

114
00:07:59,922 --> 00:08:00,822
What's that mean?

115
00:08:01,262 --> 00:08:04,162
No matter what I do, things always turn into a disaster.

116
00:08:05,382 --> 00:08:08,142
It's like the world punishes me for even trying.

117
00:08:09,842 --> 00:08:10,242
But...

118
00:08:10,242 --> 00:08:11,122
Sorry.

119
00:08:12,562 --> 00:08:13,082
Hey!

120
00:08:18,422 --> 00:08:21,742
And just when she was finally coming back to her senses...

121
00:08:21,742 --> 00:08:23,962
This is worse than our journey to the mountains.

122
00:08:23,962 --> 00:08:27,562
Guys, am I crazy or did she just quit Franshu-shu?

123
00:08:28,262 --> 00:08:29,062
Oh, no!

124
00:08:33,282 --> 00:08:38,022
How have things been going?

125
00:08:39,122 --> 00:08:40,982
Well, they're going.

126
00:08:41,402 --> 00:08:45,902
When you first told me about your plan, I thought your damned brains must have gone rotten.

127
00:08:46,602 --> 00:08:47,942
What did you call it again?

128
00:08:47,942 --> 00:08:53,062
The original Zombie Village, Hezen's Highway Dream Project, or something like that?

129
00:08:53,242 --> 00:08:55,362
It's called the Zombieland Saga Project.

130
00:08:56,282 --> 00:08:57,222
That's the one.

131
00:08:57,822 --> 00:08:58,722
Have compassion.

132
00:08:59,422 --> 00:09:01,142
Act for the sake of man, right?

133
00:09:02,302 --> 00:09:03,502
Yeah, Hagakure.

134
00:09:04,042 --> 00:09:04,762
Great book.

135
00:09:05,762 --> 00:09:07,462
But this isn't that noble.

136
00:09:08,122 --> 00:09:09,882
Just keep your hands off, you giddy.

137
00:09:10,282 --> 00:09:12,022
I owe a hell of a lot to that woman.

138
00:09:12,542 --> 00:09:13,722
How old are you?

139
00:09:14,662 --> 00:09:15,182
Hmm.

140
00:09:15,462 --> 00:09:17,842
I sure had some interesting times back then.

141
00:09:18,202 --> 00:09:20,182
It isn't good to dwell on the old days.

142
00:09:21,142 --> 00:09:22,342
Makes you uncool.

143
00:09:22,722 --> 00:09:24,002
You're one to talk.

144
00:09:24,002 --> 00:09:30,502
Man, this sucks.

145
00:09:31,162 --> 00:09:32,882
I can't even get into the music.

146
00:09:33,622 --> 00:09:35,962
How can we during a crisis like this?

147
00:09:36,962 --> 00:09:40,462
Guys, do you think Sakura's gonna forget about me forever?

148
00:09:42,042 --> 00:09:43,722
Look, I know this is upsetting.

149
00:09:44,142 --> 00:09:47,882
But if the rest of us don't stay strong, then the whole thing falls apart.

150
00:09:48,702 --> 00:09:49,962
The show must go on.

151
00:09:50,282 --> 00:09:52,382
It's not like the audience knows our problems.

152
00:09:52,382 --> 00:09:54,502
Yeah, but still.

153
00:09:54,642 --> 00:09:55,482
It'll be okay.

154
00:09:56,122 --> 00:09:57,702
We've got to trust Sakura.

155
00:09:57,702 --> 00:10:22,462
Man, I'm all gross and sweaty.

156
00:10:24,282 --> 00:10:25,042
One sec.

157
00:10:25,222 --> 00:10:26,682
I need to go wash off.

158
00:10:26,682 --> 00:10:30,982
I'm not gonna change my mind.

159
00:10:31,202 --> 00:10:33,802
But you were so worked up about it before now.

160
00:10:33,942 --> 00:10:34,942
Well, what can I say?

161
00:10:35,022 --> 00:10:36,442
I guess I wasn't myself.

162
00:10:36,742 --> 00:10:37,842
Just forget it.

163
00:10:37,902 --> 00:10:38,962
Stop being selfish.

164
00:10:39,382 --> 00:10:40,102
I'll kill ya.

165
00:10:40,302 --> 00:10:42,402
You're just wasting your breath at this point.

166
00:10:42,662 --> 00:10:45,082
Doesn't matter how much you stomp your feet and yell at me.

167
00:10:45,162 --> 00:10:46,582
I've already made my decision.

168
00:10:47,922 --> 00:10:49,662
I've heard enough, smartass.

169
00:10:49,662 --> 00:10:55,782
Stop it.

170
00:10:55,782 --> 00:10:58,722
I said quit!

171
00:10:58,722 --> 00:11:09,162
I can't sleep.

172
00:11:09,162 --> 00:11:11,302
I'll listen to some nature sounds.

173
00:11:13,982 --> 00:11:14,862
Hey there.

174
00:11:14,862 --> 00:11:17,662
If you have something to say, just say it.

175
00:11:17,662 --> 00:11:19,662
Um, well...

176
00:11:19,662 --> 00:11:27,102
What's that?

177
00:11:27,102 --> 00:11:29,722
I think the stars are calling me.

178
00:11:29,722 --> 00:11:31,582
I'll go look at the sky.

179
00:11:33,582 --> 00:11:37,762
Sakura, I can't believe you don't remember me.

180
00:11:38,102 --> 00:11:39,002
You're so young.

181
00:11:39,102 --> 00:11:39,682
That's right.

182
00:11:39,742 --> 00:11:41,102
I'm 12 years old forever.

183
00:11:41,582 --> 00:11:42,282
It's magic.

184
00:11:42,642 --> 00:11:43,242
That's good.

185
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:44,722
So you'll stay cute.

186
00:11:45,202 --> 00:11:46,922
Like that star thing you're holding.

187
00:11:47,242 --> 00:11:47,622
Uh-huh.

188
00:11:48,062 --> 00:11:50,742
You told me my star was cute before, too.

189
00:11:50,862 --> 00:11:52,602
And you said you liked my smile.

190
00:11:53,282 --> 00:11:55,882
I had lots of fun doing idol stuff together.

191
00:11:56,402 --> 00:11:57,962
And I think you're cute, too.

192
00:12:00,442 --> 00:12:00,882
Really?

193
00:12:01,602 --> 00:12:02,982
What if I were the star?

194
00:12:03,042 --> 00:12:04,022
Does it look good then?

195
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:06,122
You're doing it wrong.

196
00:12:06,122 --> 00:12:08,302
If you're cute, those details don't matter.

197
00:12:08,842 --> 00:12:10,362
But the harder I try to be cute,

198
00:12:10,462 --> 00:12:12,342
the dumber and uglier I end up looking.

199
00:12:13,722 --> 00:12:15,702
Because I'm a failure!

200
00:12:20,542 --> 00:12:21,962
For the last time,

201
00:12:22,422 --> 00:12:24,902
I'm not going to be an idol.

202
00:12:25,882 --> 00:12:35,782
Well, it's time.

203
00:12:35,962 --> 00:12:37,782
I suppose I must begin preparations.

204
00:12:37,782 --> 00:12:51,802
Lady Sakura,

205
00:12:51,802 --> 00:13:01,802
the city's best courtesan is here.

206
00:13:01,802 --> 00:13:07,762
Oh, she's gone.

207
00:13:23,762 --> 00:13:25,642
Where did that nerd run off to?

208
00:13:25,642 --> 00:13:27,002
How troubling.

209
00:13:27,402 --> 00:13:28,042
Hang on.

210
00:13:28,382 --> 00:13:29,522
The mud's gone, too.

211
00:13:29,802 --> 00:13:31,982
Some dogs are known to sense people's emotions.

212
00:13:32,342 --> 00:13:34,262
But I don't think Romero's that clever.

213
00:13:36,742 --> 00:13:37,222
Whoa!

214
00:13:37,622 --> 00:13:38,462
What is this?

215
00:13:38,482 --> 00:13:39,862
Some kind of zombie intervention?

216
00:13:39,862 --> 00:13:47,022
They don't realize it,

217
00:13:47,242 --> 00:13:48,522
but this is for the best.

218
00:13:49,442 --> 00:13:50,342
If I stayed,

219
00:13:50,802 --> 00:13:52,602
I would just ruin everything.

220
00:13:52,602 --> 00:13:55,602
In third grade,

221
00:13:55,682 --> 00:13:56,602
we put on a play,

222
00:13:57,242 --> 00:13:58,842
and I got the lead part.

223
00:13:59,742 --> 00:14:02,162
It was a lot of responsibility for a kid,

224
00:14:02,162 --> 00:14:05,422
but I rehearsed the role every night in my room

225
00:14:05,422 --> 00:14:07,622
until I could recite all of my lines

226
00:14:07,622 --> 00:14:09,382
without making a single mistake.

227
00:14:10,902 --> 00:14:12,682
Then, the day of the show,

228
00:14:13,682 --> 00:14:15,242
even though I'd had all my shots,

229
00:14:15,942 --> 00:14:17,162
I ended up getting sick

230
00:14:17,162 --> 00:14:18,802
and had to stay home anyway.

231
00:14:20,102 --> 00:14:21,162
Bad memories.

232
00:14:21,162 --> 00:14:25,042
For fourth grade field day,

233
00:14:25,562 --> 00:14:27,562
I got picked to be on the relay team,

234
00:14:28,282 --> 00:14:30,942
so I stayed up late every night to practice

235
00:14:30,942 --> 00:14:34,062
until I had the fastest time in the whole school.

236
00:14:34,842 --> 00:14:36,142
But the day of the race,

237
00:14:36,702 --> 00:14:38,822
I somehow managed to pull a muscle

238
00:14:38,822 --> 00:14:40,082
at opening ceremonies

239
00:14:40,082 --> 00:14:41,382
and had to forfeit.

240
00:14:44,582 --> 00:14:46,462
Each year, I kept working hard

241
00:14:46,462 --> 00:14:47,722
so I could make a comeback,

242
00:14:47,722 --> 00:14:49,842
and I made relay team

243
00:14:49,842 --> 00:14:51,242
in fifth and sixth grade, too.

244
00:14:52,242 --> 00:14:52,942
But of course,

245
00:14:53,622 --> 00:14:54,822
I always pulled a muscle

246
00:14:54,822 --> 00:14:56,482
before the race ever got started.

247
00:14:57,942 --> 00:14:59,222
More bad memories.

248
00:15:00,502 --> 00:15:02,162
Fast forward to middle school.

249
00:15:02,962 --> 00:15:03,542
All summer,

250
00:15:03,642 --> 00:15:05,542
I crammed for high school entrance exams.

251
00:15:06,402 --> 00:15:09,202
I wanted to erase the bad luck I'd had before,

252
00:15:09,562 --> 00:15:11,702
so I tried to get into the best school

253
00:15:11,702 --> 00:15:12,542
in the prefecture.

254
00:15:13,302 --> 00:15:14,822
I didn't keep up with music,

255
00:15:15,202 --> 00:15:16,782
TV, my friends,

256
00:15:16,782 --> 00:15:18,822
or anything else I used to love.

257
00:15:19,502 --> 00:15:21,682
I spent my entire middle school career

258
00:15:21,682 --> 00:15:22,602
hitting the books.

259
00:15:23,882 --> 00:15:25,602
And because of my hard work,

260
00:15:25,922 --> 00:15:28,182
I got an A on the mock exam.

261
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:31,202
Then the real one came.

262
00:15:32,062 --> 00:15:34,162
As I was leaving the hotel I had stayed at

263
00:15:34,162 --> 00:15:35,862
to be closer to the testing location,

264
00:15:36,582 --> 00:15:37,782
I ran into not one,

265
00:15:38,262 --> 00:15:39,682
but multiple old ladies

266
00:15:39,682 --> 00:15:41,242
who were having some kind of trouble.

267
00:15:41,242 --> 00:15:45,942
I made it to the test in the nick of time,

268
00:15:46,142 --> 00:15:48,422
but I was all frazzled during the exam

269
00:15:48,422 --> 00:15:49,862
and kept making mistakes.

270
00:15:50,742 --> 00:15:52,822
So I didn't get into my top school.

271
00:15:54,522 --> 00:15:56,142
One of the worst memories.

272
00:15:58,522 --> 00:16:00,542
Everything I can remember is awful.

273
00:16:01,182 --> 00:16:02,122
They don't understand.

274
00:16:02,122 --> 00:16:03,962
Even if that one girl

275
00:16:03,962 --> 00:16:05,482
is the real Ai Mizuno.

276
00:16:06,402 --> 00:16:07,442
There's no way

277
00:16:07,442 --> 00:16:08,862
I'll ever become an idol.

278
00:16:10,462 --> 00:16:11,662
It's such a waste

279
00:16:11,662 --> 00:16:12,762
that you're not in a club.

280
00:16:13,322 --> 00:16:13,802
I mean,

281
00:16:13,842 --> 00:16:15,282
you're really good at sports

282
00:16:15,282 --> 00:16:16,922
and physical stuff like that.

283
00:16:17,302 --> 00:16:17,582
Look,

284
00:16:17,642 --> 00:16:19,022
I told you I'm finished.

285
00:16:19,722 --> 00:16:21,122
I might as well not bother.

286
00:16:21,662 --> 00:16:23,002
The harder I try,

287
00:16:23,102 --> 00:16:24,922
the worse everything seems to turn out.

288
00:16:25,142 --> 00:16:26,942
I just don't have what it takes,

289
00:16:26,942 --> 00:16:29,302
so it's better if I don't try at all.

290
00:16:38,842 --> 00:16:39,622
I don't know.

291
00:16:39,722 --> 00:16:40,442
I guess it's because

292
00:16:40,442 --> 00:16:41,882
I've never really thought of mistakes

293
00:16:41,882 --> 00:16:43,702
or failures as being a bad thing.

294
00:16:44,922 --> 00:16:46,522
They always end up helping me

295
00:16:46,522 --> 00:16:47,862
with whatever happens next.

296
00:16:48,242 --> 00:16:50,202
And if I want to be the best version of me,

297
00:16:50,262 --> 00:16:51,362
then I'll just have to find a way

298
00:16:51,362 --> 00:16:53,342
to overcome any hurdles, you know?

299
00:16:56,942 --> 00:17:12,822
I guess it's because

300
00:17:12,822 --> 00:17:14,442
I've never really thought of mistakes

301
00:17:14,442 --> 00:17:16,382
or failures as being a bad thing.

302
00:17:19,622 --> 00:17:21,782
I was trying my best.

303
00:17:22,642 --> 00:17:23,962
And just when I thought

304
00:17:23,962 --> 00:17:25,342
my bad luck would change,

305
00:17:25,342 --> 00:17:29,342
I died and came back as a zombie.

306
00:17:30,142 --> 00:17:31,702
Am I cursed or something?

307
00:17:33,062 --> 00:17:34,922
Hey, what are you doing out so late,

308
00:17:35,022 --> 00:17:35,642
young lady?

309
00:17:35,902 --> 00:17:37,282
Are you trying to get arrested?

310
00:17:37,482 --> 00:17:38,702
Because I'll arrest you.

311
00:17:39,182 --> 00:17:40,942
Did you run away from home or something?

312
00:17:41,062 --> 00:17:42,082
What gives, miss?

313
00:17:42,982 --> 00:17:44,162
What's the difference?

314
00:17:44,962 --> 00:17:45,702
All right.

315
00:17:46,122 --> 00:17:47,342
Come with me to...

316
00:17:49,182 --> 00:17:54,142
Not again!

317
00:17:55,342 --> 00:18:05,002
You know damn well

318
00:18:05,002 --> 00:18:06,642
this isn't where you need to be.

319
00:18:07,642 --> 00:18:08,422
Right, Sakura?

320
00:18:09,902 --> 00:18:10,142
Uh...

321
00:18:14,142 --> 00:18:14,902
And you are...

322
00:18:14,902 --> 00:18:16,482
KOTORO TATSUMI, DUMMY!

323
00:18:16,482 --> 00:18:22,382
I'm sorry.

324
00:18:22,742 --> 00:18:24,142
What are you trying to show me?

325
00:18:25,482 --> 00:18:26,542
Nijino Matsubara.

326
00:18:26,722 --> 00:18:27,642
Yeah, I know.

327
00:18:27,742 --> 00:18:28,462
The forest.

328
00:18:29,142 --> 00:18:32,322
But it's too dark out to see anything.

329
00:18:32,882 --> 00:18:34,162
That's you right now.

330
00:18:34,562 --> 00:18:34,942
Huh?

331
00:18:35,282 --> 00:18:37,082
There are bright points all around you.

332
00:18:37,742 --> 00:18:38,662
Saga may be small,

333
00:18:38,882 --> 00:18:40,602
but there's a person for every light you see.

334
00:18:41,222 --> 00:18:41,642
Uh...

335
00:18:41,642 --> 00:18:43,342
What are you getting at here?

336
00:18:43,982 --> 00:18:47,122
Just like they're waiting for the sun to rise over Nijino Matsubara,

337
00:18:47,562 --> 00:18:50,322
there are people out there waiting for you to shine as an idol.

338
00:18:52,542 --> 00:18:53,942
Two or three at least.

339
00:18:54,642 --> 00:18:56,822
Just do your concert without me, okay?

340
00:18:57,282 --> 00:19:00,322
I'm sure it'll be much better if I stay far away from it.

341
00:19:00,322 --> 00:19:02,722
And I know I don't have what it takes.

342
00:19:08,402 --> 00:19:11,282
So, you really don't want to be an idol then?

343
00:19:11,982 --> 00:19:14,662
Can you look into my eyes and tell me that honestly?

344
00:19:16,102 --> 00:19:17,322
Back then...

345
00:19:17,322 --> 00:19:28,422
I want to be just like Ai.

346
00:19:28,922 --> 00:19:30,842
She's so strong and confident.

347
00:19:32,982 --> 00:19:34,742
All right, make some noise!

348
00:19:34,742 --> 00:19:35,162
Woo!

349
00:19:37,162 --> 00:19:39,802
I wonder if I'll ever shine as bright as her.

350
00:19:39,802 --> 00:19:45,462
This is it!

351
00:19:45,722 --> 00:19:47,362
I'm gonna try one more time!

352
00:19:47,782 --> 00:19:49,742
I can't be afraid to give it my best!

353
00:19:58,442 --> 00:20:00,362
And look at how well that turned out.

354
00:20:01,962 --> 00:20:04,962
I should have known I'd fail at that just like everything else.

355
00:20:05,542 --> 00:20:07,282
That the best choice was to give in.

356
00:20:07,282 --> 00:20:11,102
But I was stupid and got my hopes up about being an idol.

357
00:20:11,822 --> 00:20:13,962
So I rushed out of the house earlier than usual.

358
00:20:14,422 --> 00:20:15,462
And then boom, dead.

359
00:20:16,022 --> 00:20:17,182
That's just who I am.

360
00:20:18,582 --> 00:20:22,062
But you came back to life as an idol who can save Saga.

361
00:20:22,622 --> 00:20:24,242
What makes you think that'll happen?

362
00:20:24,782 --> 00:20:25,862
And why me?

363
00:20:26,222 --> 00:20:28,622
I mean, I never asked to become a zombie!

364
00:20:28,882 --> 00:20:31,102
One day you'll understand all of those things.

365
00:20:31,182 --> 00:20:31,862
Don't give me hope!

366
00:20:32,262 --> 00:20:34,702
Hope is what got me killed in the first place!

367
00:20:34,702 --> 00:20:36,942
How bad can one person's luck be?

368
00:20:37,282 --> 00:20:40,102
If you want to do this idol thing, then go right ahead!

369
00:20:40,202 --> 00:20:41,582
But leave me out of it!

370
00:20:47,162 --> 00:20:48,282
I just...

371
00:20:48,282 --> 00:20:50,882
Don't want to be dragged into this, okay?

372
00:20:52,462 --> 00:20:53,302
Well, alright.

373
00:20:53,822 --> 00:20:55,022
Then go wherever you want.

374
00:20:55,982 --> 00:20:58,662
If you're determined to spend your life this way...

375
00:20:58,662 --> 00:20:59,742
Afterlife, whatever!

376
00:20:59,742 --> 00:21:02,962
Then please, don't let me stop you!

377
00:21:07,082 --> 00:21:08,562
I know I'm doomed.

378
00:21:09,062 --> 00:21:10,642
You didn't have to rub it in.

379
00:21:14,342 --> 00:21:18,642
If I had had any choice in the matter, I would have never come back in the first place.

380
00:21:18,742 --> 00:21:19,582
Did you miss me?

381
00:21:19,582 --> 00:21:20,962
Aw, come on!

382
00:21:21,002 --> 00:21:24,242
Did you really think I'd let your little pity party go on all night long?

383
00:21:24,322 --> 00:21:25,062
Get lost!

384
00:21:25,282 --> 00:21:26,142
You don't know anything!

385
00:21:26,282 --> 00:21:27,622
It's not like you've died before!

386
00:21:27,842 --> 00:21:28,402
You don't know how I feel!

387
00:21:28,402 --> 00:21:30,482
I have what it takes!

388
00:21:31,242 --> 00:21:34,522
Whether or not you have what it takes is irrelevant, because I do!

389
00:21:34,642 --> 00:21:35,242
Got it?

390
00:21:35,822 --> 00:21:38,422
And what it takes is good stuff!

391
00:21:38,582 --> 00:21:40,882
Good stuff that I definitely have, alright?

392
00:21:41,622 --> 00:21:42,662
Listen to me!

393
00:21:42,662 --> 00:21:46,822
I will never, and I mean never abandon you!

394
00:23:24,987 --> 00:23:31,787
Sakura here. Why are they bugging me when they know I can't do it? How can I go on with life if I'm dead?

395
00:23:32,647 --> 00:23:37,867
Next time on Zombieland Saga, Episode 12, Good Morning Again Saga. What does it all mean?

